From a06dd663820fa0da2bf3499fa4bcce90838a3e34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:12:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 43/43] usb_webcam: drive only the first video function of a
 camera

Some cameras have more than one UVC video function in one configuration,
like the 0c45:6d1f of the Dell XPS 15 9520 from #348: interfaces 0 and 1
are the color camera, interfaces 2 and 3 an infrared one. Only the first
streaming interface was taken, but every video control interface was
parsed. The one of the infrared function overwrote fControlIndex, its
units were added to those of the color function and the interrupt
endpoint could come from it. The picture came from the color camera, but
brightness and the other controls went to the infrared one.

Take only the first video control interface. Its class specific header
lists the streaming interfaces of its function in baInterfaceNr[], and
the first streaming interface from that list is taken. The control
interface comes before its streaming interfaces, so the header is parsed
by then. Without a header or with an empty list, the first streaming
interface is taken as before.

The check is uvc_function_has_streaming() in UVCFunction.h, with tests
in UVCFunctionTest. Tested: the add-on and the test build for x86_64
without warnings, the test passes on the build host with ASan and UBSan.
Not tested on a camera with two video functions.

Signed-off-by: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: claude-opus-5-5
